C2  Schwarzschild: Ricci-flat, all curvature is Weyl
  [OK] R_ab == 0
  [OK] C_abcd C^abcd = 48 M^2 / r^6  (got 48*M**2/r**6)
  [OK] C^2 == Kretschmann (vacuum)
       -> a Weyl-scalar measure is unbounded at r->0 of a black hole AND of a
          white hole (time-reverse, same C^2): the scalar alone carries no arrow.
          Penrose's hypothesis supplies the arrow by FIAT (Weyl->0 at INITIAL
          singularities only); it is a boundary condition, not a derivation.

