             |E|/H^2 ~ a^-3/2
  [OK] decaying: |E|/H^2 rises iff delta rises
       -> in the one computable regime, 'clumping raises the Weyl measure' holds
          for these measures in both modes; it is Poisson's equation, and it
          says nothing about whether C-based measures ARE an entropy.

